            <ArticleTitle>Forget Me Not: A Case of Gossypiboma (Textiloma) Mimicking an Orbital Tumor.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e5-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/IOP.0000000000000406</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Retained foreign bodies are not infrequent following surgical procedures and are associated with medico-legal issues. Gossypiboma following ocular surgeries is rare but should be included in the differential diagnosis of a postoperative patient presenting with pain or mass. We report on one such case of gossypiboma following surgical excision of lacrimal gland.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
